      "description": "Follie™ — The All-in-One Anesthesia Reference for Students and Clinicians\n\n600+ procedures. 1,300+ comorbidities. 250+ drugs. One app built by a clinician who knows what you actually need at the bedside.\n\nPrep smarter. Study faster. Walk into every case with confidence.\n\nANESTHETIC PLAN GENERATOR (Patent Pending)\nEnter patient data across 8 pages and Follie generates a complete anesthetic plan. 600+ procedures across 20+ specialties. All on-device, all instant.\n\nCOMORBIDITIES\n1,300+ conditions with anesthetic implications and structured preop/intraop/postop guidance — cardiac, pulmonary, neuro, endocrine, rheumatologic, psychiatric, and more.\n\nEMERGENCY PROTOCOLS\nWeight-based dosing for ACLS, PALS, MH, anaphylaxis, and LAST. Crisis checklists. Screen stays awake during emergencies.\n\nDIFFICULT AIRWAY ALGORITHM\nInteractive decision tree with FOI vs video laryngoscopy guide, SGA device comparison, obesity/OSA airway considerations, and post-extubation management.\n\nMULTILINGUAL MEDICAL PHRASES\nEssential patient communication phrases in 10 languages — Spanish, Korean, German, French, Italian, Portuguese, Russian, Ukrainian, Arabic, and Somali — with pronunciation guides.\n\nSURGEON & ANESTHESIA TEAM CARDS\nSave preferences, temperament, teaching style, and notes for surgeons and anesthesia providers. Share cards with classmates via deep link.\n\nDRUG REFERENCE LIBRARY\n250+ anesthetic agents with dosing, onset/duration, contraindications, side effects, and clinical pearls.\n\nCLINICAL CALCULATORS\n30+ calculators — MAC, ETT size and depth, IBW/ABW/BSA, EBV and allowable blood loss, ABG interpreter, opioid conversion, RCRI, Apfel PONV, Parkland, CrCl, and more.\n\n170+ REFERENCE SHEETS\nComorbidities, subspecialty anesthesia, pharmacology, monitoring, emergency protocols, ICU management, bedside procedures, physiology, and more — all in original, student-friendly language.\n\nMEDICAL TERMINOLOGY\n1,000+ searchable medical abbreviations A-Z with quick-jump sidebar.\n\nQUICK HANDOFF & OCR\nDocument medications given, fluids, invasive lines, regional anesthesia, and vitals for PACU handoff. Scan medication lists, allergies, and surgical history with your camera.\n\nCASE LOGGING\nTrack cases by procedure, anesthetic type, techniques, rotation, and role. Export to CSV.\n\nADDITIONAL TOOLS\nSign in with Apple or Google to sync across devices. PDF export. Pre-op checklist. Board prep. Red screen mode. ASRA anticoagulation timing. NPO guidelines. ASA classification guide. 40+ regional block references.\n\nCLINICAL INTEGRITY\n150+ individually cited references from Miller's, Stoelting's, Barash, ASA, ASRA, AHA, ACC/AHA, AABB, and more.\n\nWHO IT'S FOR\nAnesthesia students, residents, and practicing clinicians. Whether you're prepping for your first intubation or your thousandth, Follie has your back.\n\nSUBSCRIPTION\nFollie is free to download. Full access is available as a subscription or a one-time purchase:\n• Monthly — $7.99 per month\n• Annual — $49.99 per year\n• Lifetime — $99.99, one payment, no renewal\nNew subscribers get a 7-day free trial. Subscriptions renew automatically unless cancelled at least 24 hours before the period ends.\n\nALREADY BOUGHT FOLLIE? IT STAYS YOURS.\nIf you purchased Follie before it moved to a subscription, your access is permanent and you do not need to pay again.\n\nBuilt with care by Attuned Labs LLC.\n© 2026 Attuned Labs LLC. All rights reserved.\nQuestions or feedback? follie@heyattuned.com\n\nLicensing Agreement (Apple): https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/\nTerms of service: https://heyfollie.com/terms\nPrivacy policy: https://heyfollie.com/privacy\n\nDisclaimers:\n1. Follie is an educational reference tool, not a substitute for professional medical judgment. Always consult a qualified provider before making clinical decisions.\n2. Some features may be offered as separate subscriptions in future updates.",
